    "totalDuration": "17 yrs 11 mos",
    "description": "• Developed key components of WH’s C++ low latency trading engine, including market data processing, order entry exchange connectivity, trading strategies, and a Qt-based front end.\n• Collaborated with traders to define and implement quoting strategies (pricing models and market entry), hedging techniques, order management (stacking and aggregating), and rapid market exiting.\n• Led exchange connectivity projects writing to CME, ICE (Liffe), Eurex, Euronext, CBOE Futures Exchange (CFE), NFX, SGX, and Direct Edge.\n• Led an FPGA project to evaluate custom tick-to-quote, fill-to-hedge, and tick-to-cancel solutions achieving sub-microsecond latencies.\n• Integrated SolarFlare’s TCPDirect API and validated latency savings compared to OpenOnload.\n• Designed and implemented a low-latency “FPGA Fast Cancel Server” that allowed trading systems across the firm to register different rules that when triggered would cancel their orders much faster than their trading engine could.\n• Designed and developed an API for a New York-based team to trade equities using WH’s trading engine while keeping their strategies confidential.\n• Migrated key trading functionality from an acquired trading group’s platform, reducing costs by consolidating traders onto WH’s platform.\n• Tested and validated performance metrics with nanosecond precision.\n• Developed comprehensive unit tests to validate trading engine logic, consistently maintaining one of the highest test coverage rates across the development team.\n• Mentored junior team developers, led recruiting efforts, and managed intern training programs.\n• Led Trader Open House meetings to review new software features.\n• Created User Acceptance Testing environment and tools to quickly clone production into UAT.\n• Technologies Used:\n      • C++20, Multi-threaded programming, Google Test, Disruptor Pattern, Google Protobuf, Sockets API, Multicast API, TCPDirect, Qt, Boost, SolarCapture, wireshark, Git, Linux•",
